ROLASOLV® Fabric Blackout Roller Blinds are the only Flame Retardant Blackout Roller Blinds that are Type Approved for use on board Floatels, Oil Rigs, Platforms, FPSO’s, Jack-ups, Offshore Drilling Units and other Offshore Structures. Help crew get valuable rest during daylight hours with ROLASOLV®.
Apart from the environmental and cost saving benefits, the safety aspect is also extremely important. Safe operation of offshore vessels is essential to ensure an incident-free workplace – by reducing up to 93% of glare and reflection from the sun, SOLASOLV® screens are ideal for windows on the navigation bridge, control rooms, crane cabs, drill cabs, observation/operation rooms, and any windows where it is vital that operators have a completely clear view outside.
ROLASOLV® fabric roller blinds for marine interior windows are Type Approved by DNV and regularly specified for windows on floatels, rigs, accommodation platforms, FPSO’s, supply ships and other offshore and marine vessels.
Solar Solve only select the highest quality flame retardant fabrics that are stringently tested to ensure that they can withstand extremes of temperature – from arctic to tropical conditions – and are UV resistant. They have BS5438 flame spread certification and have been successfully tested to comply with the mandatory IMO (International Maritime Organization) FTPC Part 7 A.563(14) Resolution, the main fire testing standard for Textiles and Films.
The aluminium hardware and components we use are selected for their durability and their compatibility with the marine environment. The profile can be painted in a choice of 400 RAL colours with a matt or gloss finish.
