We take great care to ensure that someone’s personal contact details, which are very important to us and vital in the course of conducting our business, are accurate, safely stored and remain confidential. Personal contact information in the form of hard copy is stored in secure areas of our facility, with electronic storage being password protected.
WEBSITE COOKIES – the solasolv.com website has been created using WordPress tools and like most websites it uses cookies to collect information. Cookies are small data files which are placed on computers or other devices as you browse this website to remember things like when your computer visits our website.
PLACES WHERE PERSONAL CONTACT INFORMATION MAY BE TRANSFERRED – SSL offers a world-wide delivery service. Personal contact information, when necessary to enable an order or request for information to be completed, will be transferred globally.
Therefore, we do take contact details that normally include the person’s name, job title, telephone numbers (depending on which ones they supply us with), email address and postal address. We use that information in a number of ways: to respond to requests for quotations or other types of information; to liaise as part of SSL’s order processing contract-review; for warranty purposes, to check our records are right and to check every now and then that you’re happy and satisfied.
We don’t sell, rent or trade email lists with any other organisations or businesses.
YOUR RIGHTS OF ACCESS TO YOUR PERSONAL INFORMATION – You have the right to, (i) be informed about the personal data SSL is processing about you; (ii) get your personal data rectified and/or erased if it is incorrect and (iii) object to the processing of your personal data and have it erased.
If you are not happy with the way SSL is processing your personal contact details or the way that SSL staff have dealt with your requests, you can lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority. You can do it at any time.
