A Virtual Credit Card is a payment method that offers a line of financing so you can make purchases that you cannot (or don’t want) to pay with cash.
A virtual credit card works exactly the same as a physical one, but is only for e-commerce.
Virtual cards Visa и Mastercard Is a payment method that is gaining more and more place among banks around the world. The idea is to generate a non-physical version of the card for online payments only.
Virtual cards Visa и Mastercard aimed at improving the security of online shopping
The following are the main features of the virtual card:
Each type of virtual cards has its own characteristics:
Temporary Virtual Card: Ideal for a one-time purchase, such as online shopping or over the phone. This card has its advantages:
• Does not provide physical map data on the Internet.
• Valid for a one-time online purchase.
Recurring Virtual Card: Suitable for recurring purchases such as subscriptions (eg streaming, gym), shipping and transportation services, and other services where you save your card for future purchases (eg digital wallets). Among the advantages of this type of cards are:
One of the ways to avoid possible fraud is to create a virtual credit card, since in this case you will never provide the merchant with your real card details, and the limits on the use of these cards are predetermined by you. Since gamblers can create a virtual card for every payment at an online casino, they need to know how to create one.
Features: You do not need to activate the virtual card, it is already available in the banking application in the "My credit cards" section, and you do not need a password to use it.
Safety: The security code on the virtual card changes frequently, which greatly complicates the possibility of fraud or compromise of card data.
Convenience: You can make online payments even before you receive the physical card, as it is available within two days of ordering the physical form.
Convenience: If you lose your physical card, the virtual card will continue to function normally.
Exemption from commission: The card has no commission or annuity.
