After vision of Christ, Nigerian bishop credits Rosary for victories against Boko Haram
Now, as the Nigerian army boasts it has rooted the insurgents out of their last strongholds and pushed them into the Sambisa forest, Bishop Dashe Doeme is claiming credit for Mary. “Before, Boko Haram members were everywhere.
In it Christ gave him a sword, which immediately turned into a rosary. Christ then said, “Boko Haram is gone.” The bishop said he took Jesus’ message to be, “In order to console his people, that His Mother is there for us.”
Bishop Dashe Doeme urged the praying of the rosary daily throughout the diocese’s schools, families, and parishes.
The bishop told the Catholic Herald that the rosary “has worked wonders, has liberated nations.” Citing the Battle of Lepanto in 1571, for example, when Christian naval forces defeated the much bigger fleet of the Ottoman Empire; and in 1986,, when Philippines’ Dictator Fernando Marcos was deposed.
