I’m developing a schedule for dedication of the daily rosary, and I’d love to hear what you guys think!
I always used to be hesitant to do it, because it takes like 20 minutes and I’d rather be doing fun things. But I now feel obliged to continue praying it, and it gets easier each time.
Miraculous Medal Prayer “”O Mary, conceived without sin, pray for those who have recourse to thee.””
So I decided to develop a weekly schedule, kind of like the different mysteries. I think it will also provide accountability – I will be less likely to miss the rosary if I feel like I’m letting someone down.
Tuesday The disadvantaged: that the disadvantaged in the local area and around the world will be blessed with what they need to live, and move themselves beyond poverty.
Thursday Japan: that more Japanese people may find Christ, and that their society may be blessed. I visited Japan last September, and basically ever since, I have prayed every day for their country and the people I met.
Saturday Life: that the life of all humans will be protected from evils such as abortion, euthanasia, and war. I’d like to know what /r/Catholicism thinks.
I still don’t know what I want to be when I grow up, but I know I want it to be spelled right and punctuated correctly. I guess that’s something.
