Firefighters carry the restored statue of the infant Jesus that they saved from the wreckage a year before.
The Shrine of Christ the King Church in Woodlawn held an event on Saturday morning to commemorate the anniversary of last year’s fire that severely damaged the historic building.
After mass, Reverend Canon Matthew Talarico led the group of more than 100 people across the street, where he delivered a speech recognizing the many people who had made it possible to save the Shrine.
Among those recognized were the community groups who had rallied to save the church from demolition, including the Coalition to Save the Shrine, the nearby churches that had shared their space with the Shrine’s congregation, the Archdiocese of Chicago, and the firefighters who battled the blaze.
