Did Jesus Condemn Formula Prayers Like the Rosary?
In this passage, one could conclude that Jesus believes anyone who “babbles” on and on saying the same words during prayer are “pagans.” Is that true?
Let’s look closer at that passage.
“Do not be like them. Your Father knows what you need before you ask him.
Our Father in heaven,
on earth as in heaven.
So Jesus teaches His disciples a “formula prayer” that they must pray in direct contrast to the pagans. Didn’t Jesus condemn formula prayers?
–battalagesete, which means to stammer, babble, prate, or to repeat the same things over and over mindlessly) as the Gentiles do…We have to remember that the main idea of prayer and sacrifice among the pagans was to appease the gods so that you could go on with your own life. You had to be careful to ‘take care of’ all of the gods by mentioning them, and saying all the right words, lest you bring a curse upon yourself.”
Which brings up the rosary and other repetitive prayers. The reason why these prayers are different is because they are born out of love for God and who would say that we shouldn’t tell God how much we love Him?
Would they get annoyed if you said it every day, multiple times throughout the day?
Should I refrain from saying I love her and reduce it to only once a day?
Nor should we pray the rosary because we believe that Mary will calm God’s temper. Our prayers should be born out of love of God and that is the secret to the power of the rosary and other formula prayers.
