The permits for four Mriehel tower blocks and Town Square mega high-rise development are set to be granted this Thursday. Join NGOs Flimkien ghal Ambjent Ahjar, Din l-Art Helwa, Friends of the Earth (Malta) and Ramblers in voicing the public’s concerns relating to these damaging projects at the Planning Authority hearing by booking a place at the Planning Authority hearing on 22902018.
Building high-rise towers is not a case of “Better build up than out” into the countryside, as those wanting a farmhouse/weekend getaway in ODZ will not simply buy a high-rise apartment instead. The proof of this is that in spite of all the tall buildings being proposed, the number of countryside applications is at a record high.
Tall buildings deprive residents of light, air and solar rights, and will change Malta’s landscape for ever, ruining heritage vistas like the view of Mdina which will impact Malta’s tourism appeal. Mriehel was included in the high-rise policy underhandedly, after the public consultation had closed.
