(mm) Connection Working Length
In conventional diamond core drill bits, diamonds are arranged randomly and disorderly in the metal matrix. In the diamond-enriched area, the diamond concentration is high, and the drilling force of a single diamond is small, and it is easy to be polished and worn.
Therefore, drill bits with disorderly arrangement of diamonds have the problems of low cutting efficiency, short lifespan, and contradictions between sawing efficiency and lifespan.
On the drilling process, each diamond bears the same drilling force, and the impact force it bears is also the same when it enters the working state from idling.
Thus, it can be concluded that the sharpness and lifespan of the diamond saw blade are improved, and the diamond concentration is reduced, and the cost is saved.
